# SHEER - what goes into the public repository is a WHITELIST: everything at the top level is ignored except the
# entries below. (Private working material - notes, drafts, reference footage of the original demo, review sheets,
# local tools, builds - stays out; the players are published as GitHub Release assets, not in git.)
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!/docs/
!/unity/
!/tools/
!/blender/

# Unity: the project's sources only (Library, Temp, Logs, UserSettings, obj and build outputs are generated)
/unity/*
!/unity/Assets/
!/unity/Packages/
!/unity/ProjectSettings/

# tools: no frames of the original video, no regenerable meshes / caches / compiled helpers
/tools/sim/ref_data/forensic/
/tools/sim/ref_data/meshes_r16/
/tools/sim/ref_data/track/
/tools/sim/ref_data/*.py
/tools/sim/ref_data/*.sh
/tools/sim/ref_data/replay_session_*.json
/tools/sim/_*
/tools/sim/*.so
/tools/audio_gen/out/

# blender (the earlier offline pipeline): scripts only
/blender/data/
/blender/dev/

# everywhere
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.blend1
.DS_Store
